# Tech Stack: Zod and shadcn/ui

## Before Adding Dependencies

Before introducing Zod or shadcn/ui, check:

- `package.json` / `package-lock.json`
- `components.json` (shadcn/ui)
- `components/ui/` (existing UI components)
- Existing validation code (e.g. `lib/**/parser.ts`)

If already installed or initialized, **do not add them again**.

Current project status:

- **Zod**: installed (`zod` in `package.json`)
- **shadcn/ui**: initialized (`components.json`, `components/ui/`, `lib/utils.ts`)

## Zod

Use Zod for validation of:

- User input (forms, query parameters)
- External data (API responses, webhooks)
- Data parsed before database operations

Prefer Zod schemas over ad-hoc regex or manual checks for new validation logic.
When refactoring existing parsers, migrate to Zod only when it is part of the current task.

## shadcn/ui

Use shadcn/ui as the foundation for UI components.

- Initialize according to the existing project setup (`components.json`, Tailwind in `app/globals.css`, `@/` aliases).
- Add only the components needed for the current task (`npx shadcn@latest add <component>`).
- Do not bulk-add unused components.
- Place components under `components/ui/` and compose them in feature components under `components/`.
- Reuse existing UI components before adding new ones.
